OL,3,GNEWSACode cracked for shipwreck padlock
OL,4,Asolving 400-year-old mystery
OL,5,
OL,6,FExperts have cracked a four-letter code
OL,7,Fto open an ancient padlock from a
OL,8,Fshipwreck off the Welsh coast using
OL,9,Fmodern scanning technology.
OL,11,FThe 400-year-old brass lock was
OL,12,Fdiscovered by metal detectorist Peter
OL,13,FHughes in the sand near Margam in Port
OL,14,FTalbot, in 1999.
OL,16,FIt forms part of a wider treasure hoard
OL,17,Ffrom the Ann Francis ship that was
OL,18,Fcaught in a storm on 28 December 1583
OL,19,Fon the way back from Spain. Its cargo
OL,20,Fwas hidden beneath the sand for
OL,21,Fcenturies.
OL,23,APub: 03-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
